Z||000000||pherder||01-16-2000||11:44 AM||||Below are a couple of (low quality) pictures of my 88 Coupe Project.<BR>As of a week from Monday (i.e. 24 Jan) I will own one of each model Fiero made in 1988!  First was this Coupe, next is my Formula (to be made into an ARTERO, see other album), and third will be my GT.<P><BR>      <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=208525&a=1537447&p=15272717&Sequence=2">      <BR>      <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=208525&a=1537447&p=15272714&Sequence=0">      <P> <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=208525&a=1537447&p=15289608&Sequence=1"> <P> <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=208525&a=1537447&p=15289609&Sequence=0"> <P> <BR>The following is the URL of my albums. <P> <A HREF="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/AlbumList?u=208525" TARGET=_blank>http://albums.photopoint.com/j/AlbumList?u=208525</A>  <BR><p>[This message has been edited by pherder (edited 01-16-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000001||2M4 Dale||01-16-2000||11:58 AM||||Looks Great !!! Looks like fun !!! I've got my 87 Coupe in pieces at the moment, too. I'm just doing interior and body work though. Maybe next year a cool engine transplant...The Quad Four looks like a good option. GOOD LUCK||||reg||14
Z||000002||SCCA FIERO||01-16-2000||06:23 PM||||When you get that Q4 installed, you gotta autocross it and let me know how you do! With that 4 cylinder in it you will remain it E stock (no competion for you unless you consider a Civic competion  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">) <P>There is a complete Q4 HO in a local boneyard I have had my eye on... only $200 complete.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Cooter||01-16-2000||06:41 PM||||Does the Q4 bolt to the stock Fiero transmission?||||reg||1
Z||000004||pherder||01-16-2000||06:44 PM||||I don't think the fellow racers would let an engine in stock class that never was in the Fiero.<P>A/P or E/M are the classes that it would qualify for.  These are for RACING cars that have been stripped and running racing slicks.<P>Also, I have every option I could install in this car (power mirrors, power windows, power door locks, sunroof, subwoofer, roll bar (roll bar????)  I will try to get a picture of that ...) SO it would be a little heavy for AutoXing.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"><P>And, NO, the Q4 has a different bolt pattern that only the Q4 has.  Bottom line is you must use the transaxle that comes with the Q4 (or TwinCam of 96-)<P><p>[This message has been edited by pherder (edited 01-16-2000).]||||reg||11
Z||000005||sdm1964||01-17-2000||07:24 AM||||Hey what you gonna do with that TPI motor? ||||reg||1
Z||000006||pherder||01-17-2000||08:07 AM||||The TPI engine is going into my 88 Formula and the Formula is getting the PISA Artero body kit put on it.<P>First the TPI engine will be installed (it is #3 on the project list.)  I will drive it then to insure I got that part right.  Then this next winter, the Artero body kit will be installed.<P>Other Projects are (of course) the 88 Coupe (1st on the project list) and new to me, 88 GT which I have a 3.1 build to finish and then install in the GT.<BR>||||reg||4
Z||000007||ChadMan||01-17-2000||10:26 AM||||That Quad 4 looks great, especially with the polished header and exhaust!  A few questions...<P>I notice your Coupe is a manual.  Did your Quad 4 come with the 5-speed Getrag transmission?  Or did you have to find one to mate up with it?<P>What year Quad 4 is that?  Did you rebuild it?  (I heard the early Quad 4's blew head gaskets, but that GM made a fix that made the later years reliable.  No one seems to know what years are good and what years aren't, though!)<P>How much rewiring is involved in the Quad 4 swap?  Or can you use the ECM and harness from the donor car without extensive modification?<P>I bought my 88 Coupe thinking I'd one day drop in a Q4.  Then I started thinking V6...now I'm starting to think Q4 again.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000008||turbo86se||01-17-2000||10:53 AM||||Either it's my eyes because I just woke up, or is that a bright red roll-bar in the back of your coupe?  Looks awesome! The Quad Four looks awesome too! Good work!! Did you make the roll-bar yourself? Or can you buy it somewhere? <BR>Thanks!  -joel||||reg||1
Z||000009||pherder||01-17-2000||06:53 PM||||ChadMan,<P>I actually have an Isuzu 5 speed since the Getrag that was attached to this 93 HO Quad 4 was sold.  The Isuzu was attached to a 97 TwinCam from a SunFire (it is the Quad 4's new name ... and new displacement ... 2.4L)  The HO Quad 4 only had the FWD Getrag transaxle.  The newer they are (i.e. up to 1994) the harder they are to put into the Fiero since the FWD cars don't use the mounting bosses we need for the Fiero.<P>I haven't rebuilt this engine, yet, since it had about 30K miles on it and has good compression on all four.  <P>ALL Quad 4s had problems with the head gaskets.  There are two kinds of Quad 4s, ones that have had their head gaskets replaced and those who will.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif">  I don't know why people try to put turbos or superchargers on these engines with a weak link like the head gaskets?  BTW, it is the position of one of the head's water holes quite close to the piston hole that is the problem ... the gasket is so thin there that any chance the compression has to take out that piece of gasket, it does.<P>Wiring involved taking the Fiero rear harnesses and the Quad 4's harness and mating them together (tried to put them in a dark room with mood music but it just didn't work! ;^)  Some wires are shortened and some are lengthened.  I have a wiring board layout that made it easlier.  The problem I had was I did what you are not supposed to do and that was buying the parts from different cars.  I have an 93 engine, 89 ECM and wiring, a 97 transaxle and parts from several other Olds/Pontiac cars to "complete" the swap.  Not for the faint of heart!<P>I believe my V8 swap will be as much "fun" as this swap since the same things have to be done. I.e. the electronic fuel injection is basically the same only times 2 AND it have a kit to put the V8 in! The problem with the Q4 swap was I didn't use a kit, I did it myself with the help of several talented people to make the trans mounts and the exhaust system (BTW, there isn't a header there, it is the cast iron manifold!!!)<P>turbo86se,  Yes, that is a RED roll bar installed!  4 point from Kirk Engineering out of Birmingham, AL.  They sell a full roll cage also!  Had one but sold it. <P>Roll bar cost approx. $300 with the cage @ $500.<P>Paul||||reg||3
Z||000010||Cooter||01-17-2000||08:44 PM||||Get me a phone number for Kirk Eng. if you dont mind. I live about 45 minutes from Birmingham and have entertained the thought of adding a bar to my GT.||||reg||1
Z||000011||pherder||01-17-2000||09:11 PM||||Here is Kirk Racing Ad from Grassroots Motorsports magazine<BR>(opps!  not Engineering!)<P>They have a web page ... sort of ...<BR> <A HREF="http://www.kirkracing.com/" TARGET=_blank>http://www.kirkracing.com/</A> <P>WARNING!!!!!!!!<P>If you DO get a roll bar/cage from Kirk, AND you want to keep your computer cover, then you HAVE to tell them you DON'T want a SCCA legal bar!!!  As you can see in my photo of the bar, it has a diaginal bar that just clears the computer cover on the right side (left in photo) and another bar behind the driver's seat that starts straight (horizonal to the ground) and curves up to the top (you can just see the curve).  If you order a SCCA legal bar, it goes straight across from side to side at the level of the ECM!!!! (just like the picture of the cage in the ad.)  The ECM may have to be relocated and I know for sure that the cover (rear console?) would have to be extremely modified or not used at all!<P>WARNING!!!!!<P>     <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=208525&a=1537447&p=15329295&Sequence=0">     <P><p>[This message has been edited by pherder (edited 01-17-2000).]||||reg||1
